<title>TURKEY: Turkish Eregli H1 profits up 49 pct.</title>
<headline>Turkish Eregli H1 profits up 49 pct.</headline>
<dateline>ISTANBUL 1997-08-01</dateline>
<text>
<p>- Jan-June 1997 final (billion lira unless  stated)</p>
<p>    Per share profit	572.70  vs	384.76</p>
<p>    Net Profit	    3,628.69  vs    2,437.83</p>
<p>    Net sales	    67,449.31  vs   27,799.97</p>
<p>    Operating profit   19,662.04  vs    6,774.99</p>
<p>    Exceptional income  3,847.43  vs    2,068.39</p>
<p>    Interest paid	15,238.64  vs    4,300.00</p>
<p>    Total debts	 112,995.62  vs   71,404.55</p>
<p>    Equity		 68,009.49  vs   29,366.00</p>
<p>    Capital		 6,336.00  vs    6,336.00</p>
<p>NOTE- Eregli Demir Celik Fabrikalari T.A.S. is Turkey's only flat-steel  producer and partially privatised with a 51.66 percent stake held  by state.</p>
<p>The Ankara administrative court cancelled on July 29 the tender for  a partial block-sale because it was against the constitution.</p>
<p>The figures above do not take into account Turkey's 78 percent consumer  price inflation in June.</p>
<p>--Istanbul Newsroom +90-212 275 08 75</p>
</text>
